ching","public worship","sermon requirements","presbytery discipline","review of presbytery records","institutional procedure"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2023-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A BCO 40-5 citation arose from Metro New York Presbytery's failure to redress a session that allowed a woman to expound Scripture in place of the sermon preceding the Lord's Supper, held services without preaching, and celebrated the Supper without a preceding sermon. The SJC remitted the matter to the presbytery for constitutional resolution because the session's later no-exception response was clearly inadequate and the unapproved minutes were unclear. Presbytery must complete its work with TE Higgins and Trinity Presbyterian Church's session and report to the 51st General Assembly. A separate procedural note questioned the Assembly's direct referral but did not void it."}},{"id":"wlc:Q.156--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Eastern Canada: Presbytery approved an exception to WLCQ 156 in which a candidate stated he does “not see","year":2005,"disposition":"satisfactory","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"wlc:Q.156--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html:occ-efa960de264e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html","repository_path":"rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":27},"excerpt":"*Presbytery approved an exception to WLCQ 156 in which a candidate stated he…*","sources":["rpr_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/eastern-canada__010.html"},{"id